WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.290
Welcome to Enabling Virtual Work. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Make distributed work effective despite time-zone and coordination constraints.

2
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:21.500
Consider this scenario. An international team misses approvals between time zones. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:31.780
Start with two steps: Map distributed-work constraints. Then Define norms and tools. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:41.630
Continue with Operate with documented handoffs. Then Review outcomes and adjust norms. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:41.630 --> 00:01:01.890
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous remote-working charter, handoff log, collaboration metrics tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: believing video calls alone make remote work effective; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:16.140
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
